@@@!atrep

@@/ at-usfm: a syntax mapper for scripture in the USFM model,
@@/ which USX serializes as XML and OSIS closely parallels -
@@/ one dialektos, three export surfaces (usfm, usx, osis).
@@/ Built on the genos-grouped pattern: form sims carry
@@/ structure, USFM marker names ride vocabulary genoses, and
@@/ the book identity is a vocabulary-bound lemma (the USFM
@@/ book codes, with common English names as aliases - other
@@/ languages extend the alias rows). Verses are milestones
@@/ (monosims): scripture text and paragraphs flow across
@@/ verse boundaries, the classic overlapping hierarchy.
@@/ Poetry lines wrap in per-line q-level phrases so indent
@@/ levels survive the round trip.

@=== book
@# lemma=books
grammata
#@
@"book division; the lemma is the USFM book code"@
===@

@=== chapter
@##(n)
@"chapter milestone; marks a position in the flow like verses"@
===@

@=== verse
@|(n)
@"verse milestone; text flows across verse boundaries"@
===@

@=== block
@_ grammata _@
@% markers
@"typed one-line block (headings, titles, speakers, refs)"@
===@

@=== poetry
@~
stichos
~@
@"poetry block; each line wraps in a q-level phrase"@
===@

@=== phrase
@, grammata ,@
@% chars
@"character-level span; the genos is the USFM marker"@
===@

@=== note
@^ grammata ^@
@% notes
@"footnote/endnote/cross-reference, inline at its anchor"@
===@

